it alpenglow-red over Lake Torre; the signature image of Patagonia","when":"Dec-Feb","commission":"guided sunrise day-hike (Chile Nativo / EcoCamp / lodge)"},{"name":"French Valley (Valle del Frances)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"W-trek segment (guided/self-guided)","source":"https://www.swoop-patagonia.com/chile/torres-del-paine","timing":"Dec-Feb","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the middle arm of the W, waterfalls and hanging glaciers under the Cuernos","si":"expedition","blurb":"the middle arm of the W, waterfalls and hanging glaciers under the Cuernos","when":"Dec-Feb","commission":"W-trek segment (guided/self-guided)"},{"name":"Grey Glacier (boat / kayak / ice-hike)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"outfitter boat + guided kayak/ice-hike","source":"https://torres-del-paine.org/","hook":"three tiers of intimacy with a calving ice-field arm","si":"expedition","blurb":"three tiers of intimacy with a calving ice-field arm","commission":"outfitter boat + guided kayak/ice-hike"},{"name":"Lago Pehoe + Cuernos / Nordenskjold line","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"scenic day tour / lodge excursion","source":"https://www.swoop-patagonia.com/chile/torres-del-paine","timing":"Dec-Feb","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the classic postcard: the black-capped Cuernos del Paine over impossibly turquoise glacial lakes; the Pehoé viewpoint and lakeshore lodge frame it","si":"expedition","blurb":"the classic postcard: the black-capped Cuernos del Paine over impossibly turquoise glacial lakes; the Pehoé viewpoint and lakeshore lodge frame it","when":"Dec-Feb","commission":"scenic day tour / lodge excursion"},{"name":"Winter puma-tracking safari","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"luxury","commission_path":"guided winter puma program (specialist trackers)","source":"https://www.ecocamp.travel/blog/torres-del-paine-in-winter","timing":"Dec-Feb","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"May–Sep specialist trackers under windless Antarctic high-pressure skies; the counter-seasonal luxe wildlife product","si":"expedition","blurb":"May–Sep specialist trackers under windless Antarctic high-pressure skies; the counter-seasonal luxe wildlife product","when":"Dec-Feb","commission":"guided winter puma program (specialist trackers)"},{"name":"Balmaceda-Serrano fjord (Ultima Esperanza)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"outfitter day cruise from Puerto Natales","source":"https://www.howlanders.com/en/tours-chile/puerto-natales","timing":"Dec-Feb","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"full-day glacier boat from Puerto Natales to the Serrano and Balmaceda glaciers","si":"expedition","blurb":"full-day glacier boat from Puerto Natales to the Serrano and Balmaceda glaciers","when":"Dec-Feb","commission":"outfitter day cruise from Puerto Natales"},{"name":"Milodon Cave (Cueva del Milodon)","si_tag":"GEA/Heritage","tier":"essential","commission_path":"half-day tour / park-transfer add-on","source":"https://www.howlanders.com/en/tours-chile/puerto-natales","timing":"Dec-Feb","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"GEA/Heritage","when":"Dec-Feb","commission":"half-day tour / park-transfer add-on"},{"name":"Punta Arenas + Magdalena Island penguins","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"outfitter half/full-day (Oct-Mar)","source":"https://www.howlanders.com/en/tours-chile/punta-arenas/magdalena-island-penguin-tour","hook":"a boat across the Strait of Magellan to a colony of ~thousands of Magellanic penguins","si":"expedition","blurb":"a boat across the Strait of Magellan to a colony of ~thousands of Magellanic penguins","commission":"outfitter half/full-day (Oct-Mar)"},{"name":"Petrohue Waterfalls + Osorno Volcano (Lake District)","si_tag":"GEA/RHN","tier":"essential","commission_path":"full-day tour / Lake District DMC","source":"https://www.veloso.com/chile/puerto-varas/excursions/osorno-volcano-petrohue-waterfalls/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"The Osorno summit climb and Villarrica ascents require guides, crampons, ice-axe and weather windows; glaciated and crevasse-exposed. Never sold as a walk-up","si":"GEA/RHN","blurb":"The Osorno summit climb and Villarrica ascents require guides, crampons, ice-axe and weather windows; glaciated and crevasse-exposed. Never sold as a walk-up","when":"year-round","commission":"full-day tour / Lake District DMC"},{"name":"Chiloe — palafitos + UNESCO wooden churches (Castro)","si_tag":"GEA/RHN","tier":"premier","commission_path":"Chiloe DMC extension from Puerto Varas","source":"https://www.cascada.travel/blog/from-penguins-to-palafitos-everything-you-should-do-on-chiloe","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"the largest concentration of stilt houses in Chile and 16 UNESCO-listed timber Jesuit churches; curanto pit-feasts and rare mixed Humboldt/Magellanic penguin colonies at Ancud","si":"GEA/RHN","blurb":"the largest concentration of stilt houses in Chile and 16 UNESCO-listed timber Jesuit churches; curanto pit-feasts and rare mixed Humboldt/Magellanic penguin colonies at Ancud","when":"year-round","commission":"Chiloe DMC extension from Puerto Varas"},{"name":"Easter Island / Rapa Nui (moai) — remote member","si_tag":"romance","tier":"luxury","commission_path":"LATAM flight affiliate + Rapa Nui guide/lodge package","source":"https://www.micetraveladvisor.com/news/article/easter-island-chile-complete-2026-travel-guide-to-rapa-nuis-moai-sites-flights-from-santiago-and-national-park-rules/","timing":"Dec-Feb","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Folded in as a jewel and flagged remoteflag: true. It shares the subregion string but is a 5.5–6.5-hour flight from the mainland","si":"romance","blurb":"Folded in as a jewel and flagged remoteflag: true. It shares the subregion string but is a 5.5–6.5-hour flight from the mainland","when":"Dec-Feb","commission":"LATAM flight affiliate + Rapa Nui guide/lodge package"}],"faq":[{"q":"How far ahead do you need to book the Torres del Paine W-trek?","a":"Book the W-trek about 5–6 months ahead, and refugios, EcoCamp or premium lodges 6–12 months ahead for peak dates. That lead time is forced by the two-operator refugio system — Las Torres Patagonia and Vértice Patagonia release beds in stages (roughly April–June) and peak dates clear within weeks. If a date shows \"sold out,\" monitor for freed beds, as cancellations spike 2–4 weeks pre-travel.","source":"reservenature.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Which lodges make Torres del Paine a honeymoon?","a":"The all-inclusive luxe tier — explora, Tierra Patagonia and Awasi — turns the wilderness into a private-guide couples trip with villas, open bars and hot tubs facing the Cuernos. Awasi is the apex: 14 stand-alone private villas on a private reserve, each with its own dedicated guide and 4x4 for bespoke daily excursions.","source":"awasi.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What does \"all-inclusive\" mean at a Patagonia lodge?","a":"It means one nightly rate bundles lodging, all meals, open bar and daily guided excursions — structurally the same all-inclusive lane TWW tracks in the Caribbean, expressed as wilderness luxe rather than beach resort. explora Patagonia, Tierra Patagonia and Awasi all run this model at the park.","source":"patagonline.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"all_inclusive-model"},{"q":"Can you add Easter Island to a Torres del Paine trip?","a":"Only as its own standalone leg, not a day add-on. Easter Island (Rapa Nui) is a LATAM-monopoly flight of 5.5–6.5 hours from the mainland, with its own FUI entry form, a ~USD 80 park ticket (10-day validity) and a mandatory local guide inside the park. It shares the sub_region string but is 3,700 km out in the Pacific, so price and route it separately.","source":"micetraveladvisor.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is Torres del Paine safe to visit right now?","a":"Yes — it is freely bookable. Chile sits at US State Department Level 2 (Exercise Increased Caution, last updated 2026-05-20), but that level is driven by crime and civil unrest concentrated in central Santiago, not by Patagonia, which has excellent tourist-safety records. Puerto Natales Carabineros recorded zero violent crimes against international visitors in 2025, and the Araucanía/Biobío state-of-emergency is far north of this route entirely.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-05-20","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Torres del Paine?","a":"The environment, not people. Notorious Patagonian wind — gusts of 100+ km/h — can knock a hiker off a trail, and you should expect four seasons in a day, with hypothermia a live risk even in summer plus river crossings and steep moraine. Wind and whiteout can close Base Torres and French Valley at short notice, so guided trips and buffer days materially reduce risk.","source":"blogpatagonia.australis.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is the Grey Glacier ice-hike dangerous?","a":"It runs only as a guided activity, and it is never sold unguided. Walking on the glacier requires crampons, a harness and a certified guide, with an advance reservation required — the crampons, roped travel and guide judgment are the whole safety system on a live, crevassed ice-field arm. The Grey Lake kayak among icebergs is likewise guided-only for the same cold-water and calving hazards.","source":"torres-del-paine.org, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Torres del Paine & Chilean Patagonia — W-Trek, O-Circuit, Lodges & the Lake District | TravelWell","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-CL","local_keywords":["Torres del Paine trekking","circuito W Torres del Paine","circuito O Torres del Paine reservas","qué hacer en Puerto Natales","glaciar Grey kayak","mejor época para visitar Torres del Paine","volcán Osorno Puerto Varas","pingüinos isla Magdalena Punta Arenas"],"hreflang":["en","es-CL"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"name":"explora Patagonia (Salto Chico)","type":"all-inclusive lodge in-park","earning":"luxe hotel-commission band","mor":"where contracted","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Tierra Patagonia","type":"all-inclusive lodge park-edge (Lago Sarmiento)","earning":"luxe hotel-commission band","mor":"where contracted","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Awasi Patagonia","type":"Relais & Chateaux private villas + private guide/4x4","earning":"ultra commission band","mor":"where contracted","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"EcoCamp Patagonia","type":"geodesic-dome glamping in-park","earning":"premium-package commission","mor":"operator/consortium","tier":"premium-luxe"},{"name":"The Singular Patagonia","type":"boutique fjord hotel (Puerto Natales)","earning":"luxe hotel-commission band","mor":"where contracted","tier":"luxe"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Torres del Paine & Chilean Patagonia, Chile"},"geo":{"lat":-50.9423,"lng":-73.4068}}'::jsonb, 112),
  ('tortuguero-costa-rica', '10S', 'Tortuguero', 'Costa Rica', 'Canals and the green turtle nesting coast', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'Costa Rica', '{"expedition","river"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Boat-only access — no road reaches the village; arrive via La Pavona/Moín boat or TTQ airstrip + boat transfer","~22,500 green-turtle females nest annually — top green-turtle nesting site in the Western Hemisphere","Green turtle nesting Jul 1–Oct 15 (peak Jul–Aug, hatch Sep–Oct); leatherback Feb–Apr","Freshwater canal network (''Little Amazon''): 442 birds, 138 mammals, 118 reptiles, 58 amphibians","Sea Turtle Conservancy (est. 1959, Dr. Archie Carr) runs the world''s longest continuous sea-turtle research project here"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","nearest_hospital":"Hospital de Guápiles (+506 2710 6801); San José (CIMA / Clínica Bíblica) for major trauma","advisory_level":"L2","advisory_note":"Exercise Increased Caution — crime, rip currents; updated Apr 2, 2026","book_enabled":true,"air_access_verified":true,"remote_flag":true,"hazards":["boat_safety_canals","guided_only_turtle_tours_no_flash","heat_humidity","caiman_crocodile_no_swimming","rip_currents_beach"],"health":{"malaria":"low/negligible (flag: consult provider; residual Caribbean/Limón zone)","dengue":"primary mosquito risk; wet-season spike May–Nov; use repellent","water":"bottled/filtered in remote lodges"}},"timing":{"curve_start":"late June / early July","peak":"Jul-Aug (nesting) into Sep-Oct (hatching + drier micro-season)","seasonality_note":"Inverts national dry-season pattern; driven by green-turtle nesting Jul-Oct; leatherback Feb-Apr; Caribbean coast wettest but Sep-Oct comparatively drier here","booking_lead":"weeks ahead; night tours capped 15/visit, same-day lottery","fire_date":"2026-06-15 to 2026-06-22 (primary); secondary ~mid-August","flag":"biological not event-driven; sharpen on live tracking"},"jewels":[{"name":"Night green-turtle nesting walk (Jul–Oct)","si_tag":"GEA/Wildlife","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"lodge-package override + STC conservation add-on","source":"https://www.tortugueronationalpark.com/tortuguero-turtle-nesting-season/","hook":"GUIDED-ONLY — certified park guide legally required No white light, no flash photography, red-light only, dark non-reflective clothing, stay behind guide, 15-person cap","si":"GEA/Wildlife","blurb":"GUIDED-ONLY — certified park guide legally required No white light, no flash photography, red-light only, dark non-reflective clothing, stay behind guide, 15-person cap","commission":"lodge-package override + STC conservation add-on"},{"name":"Dawn canal boat safari","si_tag":"GEA/RCR","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"in-package or standalone boat tour via DMC/lodge","source":"https://www.entercostarica.com/attractions/national-parks-and-refuges/tortuguero","timing":"Jul-Aug  into Sep-Oct","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Guided Life vests, licensed/permitted operator, no swimming, no hand-trailing in water","si":"GEA/RCR","blurb":"Guided Life vests, licensed/permitted operator, no swimming, no hand-trailing in water","when":"Jul-Aug  into Sep-Oct","commission":"in-package or standalone boat tour via DMC/lodge"},{"name":"Kayak/canoe the caños (incl. Caño Palma)","si_tag":"RCR/GEA","tier":"essential","commission_path":"lodge activity add-on / local operator affiliate","source":"https://www.twoweeksincostarica.com/tortuguero-canals-boat-tour/","timing":"Jul-Aug  into Sep-Oct","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Can be unguided but guide advised Caiman & crocodile awareness, life vest, daylight only, avoid narrow overgrown caños solo","si":"RCR/GEA","blurb":"Can be unguided but guide advised Caiman & crocodile awareness, life vest, daylight only, avoid narrow overgrown caños solo","when":"Jul-Aug  into Sep-Oct","commission":"lodge activity add-on / local operator affiliate"},{"name":"Cerro Tortuguero viewpoint hike","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"guided-hike add-on (separate sector ticket)","source":"https://vamosrentacar.com/blog/tortuguero-national-park-guide/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"Guided or self Trail footing, heat/humidity, hydration; separate park sector ticket","si":"expedition","blurb":"Guided or self Trail footing, heat/humidity, hydration; separate park sector ticket","when":"year-round","commission":"guided-hike add-on (separate sector ticket)"},{"name":"Sea Turtle Conservancy visitor center","si_tag":"Culture/Conservation","tier":"essential","commission_path":"conservation donation + guided-visit add-on","source":"https://conserveturtles.org/project/stc-programs-research-tortuguero-costa-rica/","si":"Culture/Conservation","commission":"conservation donation + guided-visit add-on"},{"name":"Tortuguero village + Afro-Caribbean culture","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"village-stay bedbank + local F&B/tour affiliate","source":"https://www.twoweeksincostarica.com/sea-turtle-conservancy-tortuguero/","timing":"Jul-Aug  into Sep-Oct","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Jul-Aug  into Sep-Oct","commission":"village-stay bedbank + local F&B/tour affiliate"}],"faq":[{"q":"When do turtles nest in Tortuguero?","a":"Green turtles — the peak draw — nest July 1–October 15, concentrated Jul–Oct with highest activity Jul–Aug, and hatchlings emerge Sep–Oct (~60 days post-lay). The rarer leatherback window is Feb–Apr. Book weeks ahead, since tour slots are lottery-capped at 15 per visit.","source":"tortugueronationalpark.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"wildlife"},{"q":"What wildlife will you see on a Tortuguero canal safari?","a":"A lot: the canal network holds 442 bird species, 138 mammals and 118 reptiles, and a dawn boat safari routinely turns up spider, howler and capuchin monkeys, keel-billed toucans, tiger herons, spectacled caimans, three-toed sloths and river otters.","source":"entercostarica.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"How do you get to Tortuguero?","a":"By water, always — there is no passable road to the village. Arrive by boat via La Pavona or Moín, or fly the 25-min SJO→TTQ small-strip flight and finish by boat transfer. The boat isn''t a transfer detail here; it''s the whole mode of travel and touring.","source":"frommers.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"river"},{"q":"Is Tortuguero safe right now?","a":"Yes, with standard caution. Costa Rica is U.S. Level 2 — Exercise Increased Caution (crime, rip currents; updated Apr 2, 2026), and TWW keeps the book path open with L2 disclosure: stay aware, don''t display wealth, don''t resist a robbery, avoid poorly-lit beaches at night.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in a boat-only jungle?","a":"Remoteness and water. The nearest mainland hospital is in Guápiles, with San José for major trauma, and ambulances don''t reach here within standard windows — serious cases need boat + road/air evacuation. Do not swim: caimans and crocodiles patrol the canals, and the beach surf carries dangerous rip currents.","source":"internationalinsurance.com, 2026-07-06 · vamosrentacar.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What are the rules on the night turtle-nesting walk?","a":"A certified park guide is legally required — this is the one activity where a guide is the law, not a suggestion. Tours run 7–10 pm, are capped at 15 people, and demand red-light only (no white light or flash) and dark, non-reflective clothing; stay behind the guide throughout.","source":"tortugueronationalpark.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Tortuguero, Costa Rica: Sea-Turtle Nesting & the Little Amazon Canal Safari","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-06","search_language":"es-CR","local_keywords":["Parque Nacional Tortuguero","tortugas Tortuguero","tour canales Tortuguero","temporada de desove tortuga verde","cómo llegar a Tortuguero en lancha","avistamiento de tortugas guiado"],"hreflang":["en","es-CR"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["expedition","river"],"ultra":[{"property":"Tortuga Lodge & Gardens","management":"Böÿ Hotels (historically Cayuga Collection)","tier":"ultra_eco_ceiling","consortia":"Fora advisor lane; Virtuoso status unconfirmed — verify","mor":"highest in-destination","note":"146 private acres, 27 rooms incl. suites + penthouse, riverfront; no palace-ultra exists at Tortuguero"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Tortuguero, Costa Rica"},"geo":{"lat":10.5432,"lng":-83.5041}}'::jsonb, 113),
  ('tulum-mexico', '10S', 'Tulum', 'Mexico', 'Cliff-top Maya ruins and cenote diving', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Quintana Roo (Cancún & Riviera Maya)', '{"expedition","diveglobal","culture","wildlife"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Tulum ruins are the only Maya walled city built on a seaside cliff (El Castillo, Temple of the Frescoes).","Tulum sits above Sistema Sac Actun, a ~347 km interconnected underwater cave system.","Archaeological zone: 8am-5pm, last entry 3:30pm; best 8-10am.","Sian Ka''an Biosphere Reserve (UNESCO) borders the destination to the south.","Tulum''s open Atlantic-facing beaches are the worst-hit by sargassum in the Riviera Maya."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"Nearest trauma: Hospiten Riviera Maya, Playa del Carmen (+52 984 159 2200), ~60 km north; local clinics stabilize/transfer; major trauma to Cancún","advisory_level":"L2","malaria":"none in tourist Quintana Roo","yellow_fever":"none required"},"timing":{"peak":"Nov-Apr (dry season)","shoulder":"Nov & Feb (best value inside peak)","green":"Apr-Oct (heat, hurricane Jun-Nov, sargassum Apr-Aug)","price_swing_peak_pct":"40-60% above shoulder","shoulder_discount_pct":"15-25% below peak","booking_lead":{"christmas_nye":"reserve by September (Dec 20-Jan 5 fully books; NYE is the flagship premium window)","feb_mar_peak":"book by November (incl. Spring Break + Holy Week 2026 Mar 29-Apr 5)"},"holiday_event_peaks":["New Year''s Eve","Christmas week","Holy Week 2026-03-29/2026-04-05","Spring Break (March)"],"out_of_season_fill":"Apr-Oct: sell ruins/cenotes/Sian Ka''an, not a beach promise; cenote diving is weather-independent + sargassum-immune","campaign_start_trigger":"NYE/Christmas by mid-August; Feb-Mar peak by early October; Apr-Aug campaigns must not promise pristine beach (sargassum guardrail)","source":"https://casatira.com/best-time-to-visit-tulum-month-by-month-weather-crowd-guide-for-2026"},"jewels":[{"name":"Dos Ojos cavern dive (Sistema Sac Actun)","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"future","hook":"Guided cavern dives with cathedral light in the world''s longest cave system.","bookable_category":"cenote cave/cavern dive (guide required)","commission_path":"Amstar 12% / affiliate 4-8%","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/things-to-do-in-tulum/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"Guided cavern dives with cathedral light in the world''s longest cave system.","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"Amstar 12% / affiliate 4-8%"},{"name":"Gran Cenote snorkel/intro dive","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","hook":"Crystal-clear cenote with turtles and stalactites, all ages and levels.","bookable_category":"cenote tour","commission_path":"Amstar 12%; entry pass-through","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/things-to-do-in-tulum/","si":"expedition","blurb":"Crystal-clear cenote with turtles and stalactites, all ages and levels.","commission":"Amstar 12%; entry pass-through"},{"name":"Tulum ruins at opening light","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Cliff-top Maya walled city with sea views no other Maya site can match.","bookable_category":"guided cultural excursion","commission_path":"Amstar 12%; ruin entry pass-through","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/tulum-ruins-guide/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","blurb":"Cliff-top Maya walled city with sea views no other Maya site can match.","when":"year-round","commission":"Amstar 12%; ruin entry pass-through"},{"name":"Cobá jungle pyramids","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Taller jungle-clad Maya pyramids explorable by bike, ~28 mi north.","bookable_category":"guided cultural excursion","commission_path":"Amstar 12% / affiliate","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/things-to-do-in-tulum/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"Taller jungle-clad Maya pyramids explorable by bike, ~28 mi north.","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"Amstar 12% / affiliate"},{"name":"Sian Ka''an Biosphere Reserve","si_tag":"Wildlife & Nature","status":"future","hook":"UNESCO biosphere lagoon float — an eco-safari and a sargassum-proof day.","bookable_category":"eco-tour","commission_path":"affiliate 4-8% / DMC 12%; biosphere fee pass-through","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/things-to-do-in-tulum/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"wildlife","blurb":"UNESCO biosphere lagoon float — an eco-safari and a sargassum-proof day.","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"affiliate 4-8% / DMC 12%; biosphere fee pass-through"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Tulum safe to visit right now?","a":"Yes — freely bookable, no hold. Tulum sits in Quintana Roo, which carries a standard US State Dept Level 2 \"Exercise Increased Caution\" (dated 2026-05-29) for crime; stay in well-lit tourist zones after dark, especially in the downtown Pueblo. Note that Tulum is ~60 km from the nearest full trauma hospital (Hospiten, Playa del Carmen), so carry air-evac insurance.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Tulum?","a":"Sargassum above all — Tulum is the worst-hit beach stretch on the Riviera Maya, and 2026 is a record year, so beach quality is genuinely not guaranteed. Anchor the trip on ruins, cenotes and Sian Ka''an rather than a pristine-beach promise. Also plan for hurricane season (Jun–Nov), bottled water, and dengue (peak May–Nov, no malaria).","source":"deeparrival.com / cdc.gov, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is cenote and cave diving in Tulum dangerous?","a":"It demands the right certification for serious overhead-environment diving. Sistema Sac Actun and Dos Ojos are caves: cavern diving requires a certified cave/cavern guide and must stay in the daylight zone, and the dark cave zone requires full cave certification — no exceptions, no solo penetration. Observe no-fly of 18h single / 24h repetitive; the nearest chamber is ~60 km north.","source":"sssnetwork.com / mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"When should I visit the Tulum ruins?","a":"Right at the 8am opening. The archaeological zone runs 8am–5pm (last entry 3:30pm), and the 8–10am window beats both the heat and the crowds at this cliff-top walled city. Come in November or February for low crowds and ideal temperatures; Holy Week (2026: Mar 29–Apr 5) runs at full capacity and Apr–Oct heat is intense.","source":"absolute-adventure-mexico.com / mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What are the best cenotes for diving near Tulum?","a":"Gran Cenote and Dos Ojos lead — Tulum sits above Sistema Sac Actun, a ~347 km interconnected cave system, the densest cenote country in Mexico. Gran Cenote (2.5 mi from town) is an all-levels swim/snorkel/intro-dive; Dos Ojos is the marquee guided cavern dive. All are weather-independent and sargassum-immune, making them the reliable core of a Tulum trip.","source":"mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Will sargassum ruin the Tulum beaches in 2026?","a":"Be realistic: Tulum is the worst-hit stretch on the coast, its open Atlantic-facing beaches catch the full brunt, and 2026 is a record/near-record year — beach quality is not guaranteed. Don''t cancel; re-anchor. Build the trip on ruins, cenotes and the Sian Ka''an biosphere (all sargassum-proof), and for reliable sand, the Punta Maroma stretch ~1 hour north sits north of the worst.","source":"deeparrival.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"What is Tulum''s wellness scene like?","a":"It is Tulum''s defining draw — yoga, temazcal ceremonies, cenote healing and jungle spas concentrated along the beach road. A signature is a north-Tulum cove with a beachfront cenote where you swim fresh and salt water in one spot, paired with jungle wellness. Book through a boutique hotel or DMC; some of the best programs are direct-only.","source":"mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"wellness"},{"q":"Is Tulum good for a honeymoon, and where''s the luxury?","a":"Yes — it is a honeymoon icon, built on bohemian-luxe boutiques and staffed villas. On the beach road, design icons like Azulik and Our Habitas Tulum lead (many are direct-only — verify the channel); for branded ultra beyond the sargassum, Maroma (A Belmond Hotel) and the 70-villa Chablé Maroma sit ~1 hour north. Fully staffed beach villas are the top private rung.","source":"virtuoso.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Tulum, and how far ahead do I book?","a":"November–April is the dry high season; November and February are the best value inside it (roughly 15–25% below peak), with November the single best month (dry, minimal seaweed, pre-holiday prices). Peak weeks run 40–60% above shoulder — reserve Christmas/NYE by September and Feb–March by November, as the boutique scene sells out months ahead.","source":"casatira.com / boldlygo.world, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"planning"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Tulum Travel Guide 2026 — Maya Ruins, Cenotes, Sian Ka''an & Straight Sargassum | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Plan Tulum: cliff-top Maya ruins at dawn, Sistema Sac Actun cenote diving, Sian Ka''an biosphere, plus straight 2026 sargassum reality, Level 2 safety and dive-chamber contacts.","slug":"tulum-mexico","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-04","search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["ruinas de Tulum horarios","mejor época para visitar Tulum","cenotes Tulum buceo","sargazo Tulum 2026","Sian Ka''an tour","villas de lujo Tulum","hoteles boutique Tulum"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"diveglobal","status":"future"},{"si":"culture","status":"future"},{"si":"wildlife","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Maroma, A Belmond Hotel","what":"Iconic Punta Maroma beach resort, reimagined 2023, ~1h north of Tulum","why_ultra":"Belmond/LVMH flag, best regional beach north of Tulum sargassum zone","earning":"agent/consortium — on application via host-Virtuoso","virtuoso":"Virtuoso-listed (upgrade, breakfast, ~$100-200 credit, early/late)","mor":"consortium-rack — safe (green)","price_tier":"ultra","source":"https://www.virtuoso.com/travel/luxury-hotels/6163634/maroma-a-belmond-hotel-riviera-maya"},{"name":"Chablé Maroma","what":"70 pool-villa wellness retreat on Punta Maroma, cenote spa","why_ultra":"Destination-spa ultra, private-pool villas","earning":"agent/consortium — on application via host-Virtuoso","virtuoso":"Virtuoso-listed (VIP amenities)","mor":"consortium-rack — safe (green)","price_tier":"ultra","source":"https://www.virtuoso.com/travel/luxury-hotels/15885219/chable-maroma"},{"name":"Azulik Tulum","what":"Adults-only treehouse eco villas, candlelit, cenote-fed baths, Tulum beach road","why_ultra":"Singular design icon, definitive Tulum eco-ultra (polarizing)","earning":"verify — largely direct-only; on application","virtuoso":"not confirmed — treat as direct-only, flag","mor":"amber — confirm booking channel before quoting commission","price_tier":"ultra","source":"https://travel.usnews.com/hotels/review-azulik_-_adults_eco-resort_maya_spa-tulum-mexico-27488/"},{"name":"Casa Malca","what":"Former Pablo Escobar beachfront mansion, art-filled boutique hotel, Tulum beach road","why_ultra":"One-of-one provenance + curated art; boutique-ultra scarcity","earning":"on application — many beach-road boutiques direct-only; verify channel","virtuoso":"verify listing","mor":"amber — direct-only risk, confirm before net-rate","price_tier":"ultra","source":"https://casamalca.com/"},{"name":"Our Habitas Tulum","what":"Adults-only canvas-and-wood beachfront eco sanctuary, quiet Tulum beach road, reef-regeneration program","why_ultra":"Design-forward luxe-eco with strong wellness/community program","earning":"on application via host / brand TA program","virtuoso":"on Visa Signature / Mr & Mrs Smith — verify Virtuoso","mor":"confirm channel — amber","price_tier":"luxury-ultra","source":"https://www.ourhabitas.com/tulum/"},{"name":"Staffed ultra villas — Tulum beach road","what":"Fully-staffed multi-bedroom beachfront villas (e.g. 10-BR Villa Privada), chef + concierge","why_ultra":"Buy-out privacy, staffed service, direct beach access — top villa rung","earning":"commissionable via villa specialist (VOD / Journey Mexico / Isle Blue / Loco Luxury)","virtuoso":"via villa-consortium programs","mor":"commissionable-rack = safe (green); net-rate resale = flag red","price_tier":"ultra","source":"https://www.loco.luxury/villaprivada"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Tulum, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":20.2114,"lng":-87.4654}}'::jsonb, 114)
insert into public.destinations (id, region_code, name, country, line, status, depth, img, sub_region, si, feel, tier_range, price_band, draw_rank, data, position) values
  ('utila-honduras', '10S', 'Utila', 'Honduras', 'Utila Honduras diving', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'Honduras', '{"liveaboard","tropical","expedition"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["World''s cheapest PADI/SSI Open Water cert (~US$280-350), free/discounted dorm while diving; 60+ dive sites on the Mesoamerican Barrier Reef (2nd-largest on Earth)","Whale sharks year-round (best Mar-May + Aug-Sep); snorkel-only from the surface - scuba diving WITH whale sharks is prohibited","Reached by air to Roatan (RTB) or San Pedro Sula (SAP) + ferry from La Ceiba (~1 hr, ~US$35, Utila Dream ferry - sole operator); Utila airstrip is private-charter only","Budget-to-boutique dive island; ceiling = dive-resort lodge (Utila Lodge 8 over-water rooms, Mango Inn); NO branded ultra on-island - Roatan/Guanaja hold the luxury tier","The Cays / Water Cay uninhabited white-sand sandbar (Sun Jam festival site); Utila Cays Garifuna fishing village (Jewel + Pigeon/Suc-Suc); Chepes Beach; endangered Utila spiny-tailed iguana station"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (national police/fire/ambulance, Honduras - verify locally)","hyperbaric_chamber":"ON-ISLAND - Utila has its own chamber (at Utila Lodge, also doubling as island trauma center; a chamber also via Bay Islands College of Diving/College of Diving); a genuine asset most small dive islands lack","no_fly_after_diving":true,"hospital":"small clinics only + the Utila Lodge hyperbaric/trauma center on-island; serious trauma/complex dive cases route OFF-ISLAND to La Ceiba (mainland) then mainland hospital or US medevac; carry travel-medical + air-evac + DAN dive insurance","remote_flag":true,"book_enabled":true,"l3_disclosure":true,"consent_flow":{"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","disclosure_required":true,"renders":"full verbatim live US State Dept advisory for Honduras (level + reason + named-danger areas incl. Gracias a Dios L4 + the complete ''If you decide to travel'' guidance, pulled live) plus traveler acknowledgment","wording_status":"hook set only — PENDING compliance-attorney sign-off"},"state_dept_carveout":"Bay Islands (Roatan/Utila/Guanaja) explicitly noted by State as better-policed resource-concentration areas; Gracias a Dios Dept = Level 4 Do Not Travel (isolated eastern mainland); danger is mainland, away from Utila","stay_in_zone":true,"air_access_verified":"RTB (Roatan) or SAP (San Pedro Sula) international arrival, then ferry to Utila from La Ceiba (~1 hr, ~US$35, Utila Dream ferry) or Roatan-Utila ferry; Utila airstrip = private charter only; routing never touches mainland gang zones","founder_policy_note":"book_enabled rides on the BOOK WITH WARNING bin (Four-Bin v3): full verbatim live US State Dept advisory disclosed + acknowledged at booking; named danger is mainland (Gracias a Dios L4 + urban gang zones), Bay Islands carved out; keep client in-zone","reef_safety":"protected Mesoamerican marine reserve - no-touch/no-stand, reef-safe sunscreen; wall/deep-site currents; whale-shark no-touch/no-scuba boat protocol","dengue":"dengue occasionally reported on Utila - protect against daytime Aedes (DEET/picaridin)","sandfly":"sandflies/no-see-ums are the signature nuisance, most active dusk-to-dawn; standard DEET underperforms - use oil-based lotion (Skin So Soft), cover up, net/fan at night; bites rarely carry leishmaniasis","water":"tap water NOT potable - bottled/refill only; mind ice/raw produce; wash hands before eating"},"timing":{"peak":"Dec-Apr (dry season; Christmas-New Year + Easter/Semana Santa sub-peaks)","whale_shark_subpeaks":"Mar-May and Aug-Sep (year-round presence; best odds; Aug-Sep is a green-season demand spike)","shoulder_green":"late-Oct-mid/late-Feb rains + Sep-Oct highest storm risk (value trough; but Sep is a whale-shark sub-peak); value island stays busy with cert traffic","booking_window_lead_time":"TWO SPEEDS - dive-cert/backpacker = short-lead (days-to-weeks, walk-in dorms, rolling last-minute layer); over-water dive-lodge tier + peak whale-shark weeks + Christmas/Easter = 2-4 months ahead","out_of_season_fill_the_beds":"dive-cert value packages, Aug-Sep whale-shark spike at shoulder rates, freediving courses (weather-resilient), new-moon night dives, Cays day-trips between storms","holiday_event_peaks":"Christmas-New Year, Easter/Semana Santa, Sun Jam (Water Cay, ~August - verify dates), whale-shark sub-peaks as de-facto events","fire_date":"dry-peak: early-to-mid November (curve-start late-Nov minus 1-2 wks); Mar-May whale-shark: mid-February; Aug-Sep whale-shark: mid-July; dive-cert stays book-short-lead with permanent rolling last-minute layer","flag":"whale-shark sightings are probabilistic - market ''best odds'' never a guarantee; sharpen dates on live booking-pace tracking","dive_calendar":true,"sources":["https://www.utilalodge.com/whale-shark-encounters","https://www.islaguru.com/articles/utila-travel-practical-guide","https://www.mango-inn.com/","https://www.freediveutila.com/"]},"jewels":[{"si_tag":"liveaboard","name":"PADI/SSI Open Water certification (world''s cheapest)","why":"~US$280-350, free dorm while diving; the entry drug that turns a 3-day stop into a 3-week stay","timing":"Dec-Apr","tier":"essential","commission_path":"dive-operator commission on application; CLIA dive-lane convert to commissioned agent","source":"https://utiladivecenter.com/","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"dive-operator commission on application; CLIA dive-lane convert to commissioned agent"},{"si_tag":"liveaboard","name":"Night dive - ''string of pearls'' bioluminescence (Ted''s Point / Ron''s Wreck)","why":"kill the lights on a new moon and watch ostracod bioluminescence flash through the water column; hunting octopus","timing":"Dec-Apr","tier":"essential","commission_path":"dive-operator + CLIA lane","source":"https://www.dive-utila.com/advanced-open-water-diver","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"dive-operator + CLIA lane"},{"si_tag":"liveaboard","name":"Halliburton wreck + Airport Caves (deep/wall)","why":"upright cargo-ship wreck ~30 m + cavern swim-throughs full of glassy sweepers - the reef''s set-pieces","timing":"Dec-Apr","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"dive-operator + CLIA lane","source":"https://www.dive-utila.com/advanced-open-water-diver","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"dive-operator + CLIA lane"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Whale-shark snorkel expedition","why":"snorkel beside the largest fish in the ocean, year-round; captains hunt the bait-ball boil + diving birds","timing":"year-round; peak odds Mar-May + Aug-Sep","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"operator/expedition commission on application + Viator/GYG affiliate; CLIA-lane crossover","source":"https://www.utilalodge.com/whale-shark-encounters","si":"expedition","when":"year-round; peak odds Mar-May + Aug-Sep","commission":"operator/expedition commission on application + Viator/GYG affiliate; CLIA-lane crossover"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Freediving course (Freedive Utila - Central America''s freediving HQ)","why":"learn to fall through the blue on one breath at the region''s only competitive freediving cooperative","timing":"Dec-Apr","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"course commission on application","source":"https://www.freediveutila.com/","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"course commission on application"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Utila Iguana Station (endangered spiny-tailed ''swamper'' iguana)","why":"conservation center for the iguana found only on Utila, living in its mangroves - a meaningful low-cost morning","timing":"Dec-Apr","tier":"essential","commission_path":"non-commissionable conservation donation - value-add/character stop, not a margin line","source":"https://www.islaguru.com/articles/things-to-do-utila-island-honduras","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"non-commissionable conservation donation - value-add/character stop, not a margin line"},{"si_tag":"tropical","name":"Water Cay (the Cays) day-trip","why":"tiny uninhabited white-sand island + sandbar ringed by coral; snorkel-and-sandbar paradise; Sun Jam festival site","timing":"year-round, calm-day best; festival ~August","tier":"essential","commission_path":"local boat/tour operator + Viator affiliate (marine-park fee non-commissionable)","source":"https://www.utilawatersport.com/water-cay","si":"tropical","when":"year-round, calm-day best; festival ~August","commission":"local boat/tour operator + Viator affiliate (marine-park fee non-commissionable)"},{"si_tag":"tropical","name":"Utila Cays - Jewel Cay & Pigeon (Suc-Suc) Garifuna fishing village","why":"two cays joined by a footbridge, ~500 people on stilt homes over the water - a Garifuna/Caymanian fishing-village time capsule","timing":"Dec-Apr","tier":"essential","commission_path":"local boat operator + F&B affiliate-adjacent","source":"https://www.utilaguide.com/activities/cays/","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"tropical","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"local boat operator + F&B affiliate-adjacent"},{"si_tag":"tropical","name":"Chepes Beach + Rehab bar","why":"the island''s largest public beach - soft white sand, shallow calm water, beachfront bar; the free between-dives afternoon","timing":"year-round","tier":"essential","commission_path":"F&B/OTA-adjacent scene-setter, not a margin line","source":"https://www.islaguru.com/articles/things-to-do-utila-island-honduras","si":"tropical","when":"year-round","commission":"F&B/OTA-adjacent scene-setter, not a margin line"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Utila safe to visit right now?","a":"Yes, with the mandatory logged disclosure — the danger the advisory names is on the mainland, not the island. Honduras is US State Department Level 3 \"Reconsider Travel\" (issued December 10, 2024), but State''s own text carves out the Bay Islands (Roatán, Utila, Guanaja) as areas with \"a concentration of resources\" that \"are better policed,\" and Utila is reached by air plus ferry without ever touching the mainland gang zones.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2024-12-10","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"Two risks are load-bearing: mainland crime and island remoteness. The advisory names Gracias a Dios Department (Level 4 \"Do Not Travel\") and urban mainland gang zones — all away from Utila, so keep the client in-zone (airport → ferry/charter → island). Separately, serious trauma or complex dive injuries route off-island to La Ceiba then a mainland hospital or US medevac, so carry travel-medical, air-evac, and DAN dive insurance without exception.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2024-12-10","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is learning to dive here dangerous, and can I fly out afterward?","a":"Diving here rewards a certified operator and disciplined profiles, and Utila has an unusual on-island safety asset. Certify only with a PADI/SSI-certified shop (UDC, Alton''s, Parrots, College of Diving, Underwater Vision), dive within no-decompression limits, and observe no-fly-after-diving of 18–24 hours before flying. Utila has its own hyperbaric chamber at Utila Lodge (doubling as the island trauma center), with a chamber also via Bay Islands College of Diving — a genuine asset most small dive islands lack.","source":"utilalodge.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Why is Utila the cheapest place to learn to dive?","a":"Utila built its name as the place backpackers came to get certified for a few hundred dollars and never left. A PADI/SSI Open Water course runs roughly US$280–350 — among the cheapest on Earth — with free or discounted dorm accommodation while you dive, on a reef with 60+ dive sites a few fin-kicks off the dock.","source":"alongdustyroads.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"Can I dive with the whale sharks, or only snorkel?","a":"Snorkel only — scuba diving with whale sharks is prohibited. As a protected species they are approached from the surface during surface intervals: captains hunt the \"boil/roil\" of feeding fish and diving birds, and you drop off the boat and snorkel beside them. Sightings are probabilistic (best odds Mar–May and Aug–Sep) — market \"best odds,\" never a guarantee.","source":"utilalodge.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What is there to do on Utila besides diving?","a":"Plenty above the water, all budget-friendly. Take a boat to Water Cay''s uninhabited white-sand sandbar, cold cans at Chepes Beach (the island''s largest public beach), the Utila Cays Garífuna fishing village of Jewel Cay and Pigeon (~500 people on stilt homes over the water), and Freedive Utila — Central America''s first freediving training center — where you learn to fall through the blue on one breath.","source":"islaguru.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"tropical"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Utila Honduras: Cheapest Dive Certs + Whale Sharks Year-Round","meta_description":"Get PADI-certified for ~$300, snorkel with year-round whale sharks, and explore Water Cay and the Mesoamerican reef — Utila is Honduras''s budget-to-boutique dive island. When to go, how to get there, and how to stay safe.","slug":"utila-honduras","primary_keyword":"Utila Honduras diving","long_tail":["cheapest PADI certification Utila","whale sharks Utila snorkel season","how to get to Utila from Roatan La Ceiba ferry","Utila vs Roatan diving budget","Water Cay Utila day trip","Freedive Utila freediving course","Utila hyperbaric chamber dive safety"],"search_language":"es-HN","local_keywords":["buceo Utila","tiburón ballena Utila","curso de buceo Utila","certificación PADI Utila barato","cómo llegar a Utila desde La Ceiba","Cayos de Utila / Water Cay","apnea Utila (freediving)"],"hreflang":["en","es-HN"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-07"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"liveaboard","status":"live"},{"si":"tropical","status":"live"},{"si":"expedition","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Private dive charter / private liveaboard day (out of Utila)","location":"on-Utila waters","posture":"the on-island ultra move is exclusivity on the water, not a hotel - private boat/guide/whale-shark hunt","price_tier":"ultra","earning":"local operator + David''s CLIA dive lane - convert to commissioned agent where offered","mor":"commissionable only where offered; no net-rate resale","source":"https://www.utilalodge.com/"},{"name":"Roatan luxury base (branded/boutique + dive-luxury lodges)","location":"neighboring Bay Island (short ferry/flight)","posture":"the Bay Islands'' actual luxury tier - route ultra client to a Roatan base, day/overnight to Utila for whale sharks","price_tier":"ultra/luxury","earning":"Fora / host-Virtuoso lane - commission on application","mor":"no net-rate resale","source":"https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/traveladvisories/traveladvisories/honduras-travel-advisory.html"},{"name":"Guanaja private-island seclusion","location":"third/quietest Bay Island","posture":"small exclusive private-island/eco-luxury lodges - the no-crowds seclusion play","price_tier":"ultra","earning":"Fora / host-Virtuoso / CLIA - on application","mor":"no net-rate resale","source":"https://www.utilaguide.com/general/utilafaqs/"},{"name":"Utila on-island lodging","posture":"STATED PLAINLY: NO branded ultra on Utila; ceiling = comfortable dive-resort lodge (Utila Lodge / Mango Inn); sell as the whale-shark + dive day to a Roatan/Guanaja ultra base or a private charter","price_tier":"premier (ceiling)","earning":"n/a for ultra","mor":"no net-rate resale","source":"https://www.utilalodge.com/"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-07","hero":{"query":"Utila, Honduras"},"geo":{"lat":16.0983,"lng":-86.935}}'::jsonb, 115),
  ('uxmal-mexico', '10S', 'Uxmal', 'Mexico', '*If it''s a city the Maya built for the', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Yucatán (Mérida & Chichén Itzá)', '{"culture","expedition","culinary"}', '{}', '{"comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["UNESCO World Heritage since 1996; Puuc-style Maya capital, flourished 7th-10th c. AD, regional capital c. 850-950 AD","Pyramid of the Magician ~35m/100ft, rounded-corner, five build-phases, solstice-aligned; climbing banned","Open daily 8:00-17:00 (last entry ~16:00); 2026 foreign admission 556 MXN (95 INAH + 461 State)","Ecos de Uxmal light-and-sound show (4K video mapping, 2026), foreign ~748 MXN, Tue/Wed/Fri-Sun","~78 km / ~1h14 south of Mérida via Hwy 261 — a Mérida day-trip; anchor of the Ruta Puuc (Kabah, Sayil, Labná, Xlapak, Loltún)"],"safety":{"emergency_number":"911","nearest_trauma":"Mérida (~1h15 north; regional hospital hub)","advisory_level":"L1","book_enabled":true,"air_access_verified":true,"air_access_note":"MID Mérida ~1h15 drive; US nonstops incl. Houston, Miami, Dallas, Atlanta","primary_hazards":["heat/sun exposure (unshaded limestone plazas)","remote Puuc route with limited services","Loltún cave footing (guided-only)","steep Maya risers on Great Pyramid climb","dengue (rainy season)","non-potable tap water"],"climbing_note":"El Adivino climbing BANNED; Great Pyramid climbable north side"},"timing":{"inflection_curve_start":"2026-11-01","peak":"2026-12 to 2027-04","shoulder":"2026-05 to 2026-10 (hot/humid; hurricane exposure Aug-Oct)","fire_date":"2026-10-22","trigger_rule":"curve-start minus 1-2 weeks; attaches to Mérida-base lead time","booking_lead_days":{"day_tour":"2-7","merida_base_high_season":"28-84"},"event_peaks":["Hanal Pixán / Day of the Dead 2026-10-31 to 2026-11-02","summer solstice El Adivino alignment","evening light-and-sound show (dry-cool nights)"],"selling_point":"markedly less crowded than Chichén Itzá","note":"sharpen on live tracking — Mérida occupancy curves + INAH visitor counts"},"jewels":[{"name":"Pyramid of the Magician (El Adivino)","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"bundled in day-tour (guiding+transport, Host)","source":"https://yucatantoday.com/en/blog/uxmal | Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"culture","commission":"bundled in day-tour (guiding+transport, Host)","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Nunnery Quadrangle","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"day-tour inclusion","source":"https://yucatantoday.com/en/blog/uxmal | Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"culture","commission":"day-tour inclusion","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Governor''s Palace","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"day-tour + private-guide upsell","source":"https://yucatantoday.com/en/blog/uxmal | Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","when":"year-round","commission":"day-tour + private-guide upsell","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Ecos de Uxmal light-and-sound show","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"premier","commission_path":"non-commissionable ticket; drives Mérida-base room-nights","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/uxmal-light-sound-show-2026-evening-experience-guide.htm | Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"culture","commission":"non-commissionable ticket; drives Mérida-base room-nights","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Kabah — Codz Poop (Palace of Masks, ~250 Chaac masks)","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"private Puuc day-tour extension","source":"https://worldhistoryedu.com/kabah-history-and-major-facts-of-this-maya-archaeological-site/ | Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","when":"year-round","commission":"private Puuc day-tour extension","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Sayil — Grand Palace (3-story, 100+ columns)","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"Puuc day-tour extension","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/ruta-puuc-2026-kabah-sayil-labna-uxmal-circuit.htm | Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","when":"year-round","commission":"Puuc day-tour extension","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Labná — Arch of Labná","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"Puuc day-tour extension","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/ruta-puuc-2026-kabah-sayil-labna-uxmal-circuit.htm | Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"culture","commission":"Puuc day-tour extension","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Xlapak","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"premier","commission_path":"completes premium private Ruta Puuc itinerary","source":"https://en-yucatan.com/ruta-puuc/ | Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"culture","commission":"completes premium private Ruta Puuc itinerary","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Loltún caves (700m+ guided)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"GEA add-on (guiding/transport, Host); entrance non-commissionable","source":"https://yucatantoday.com/en/lolt-n-caves/ | Accessed 2026-07-06","hook":"Uneven, sometimes slick underground surfaces over a 700m+ route; entry is guided-only for safety","si":"expedition","blurb":"Uneven, sometimes slick underground surfaces over a 700m+ route; entry is guided-only for safety","commission":"GEA add-on (guiding/transport, Host); entrance non-commissionable","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Choco-Story México (Ecomuseo del Cacao)","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"add-on ticket (affiliate/Viator) + lunch upsell","source":"https://yucatantoday.com/en/blog/choco-story-uxmal-an-interactive-museum | Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"culinary","commission":"add-on ticket (affiliate/Viator) + lunch upsell","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Hacienda Yaxcopoil","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"visit add-on; private-event via Host","source":"https://www.beyondtheordinary.co.uk/features/hacienda-yaxcopoil/ | Accessed 2026-07-06","hook":"19th-C henequen estate turned atmospheric museum, on Hwy 261 en route to Uxmal; visitable and event-capable","si":"culture","blurb":"19th-C henequen estate turned atmospheric museum, on Hwy 261 en route to Uxmal; visitable and event-capable","commission":"visit add-on; private-event via Host","accessed":"2026-07-06"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Uxmal worth visiting instead of Chichén Itzá?","a":"Yes — it is the connoisseur''s Maya city. Uxmal is markedly less crowded than Chichén Itzá, with grander Puuc-style architecture: the rounded-corner Pyramid of the Magician, the lattice-stone Nunnery Quadrangle, and a Governor''s Palace whose five-acre platform carries an extended Chaac mosaic frieze. UNESCO inscribed it in 1996.","source":"mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Can you climb the pyramid at Uxmal?","a":"Partly — the distinction matters. Climbing El Adivino (the Pyramid of the Magician) is banned to protect it, but the Great Pyramid is climbable on its north side, on steep handrail-free Maya risers, so wear sturdy shoes and mind your footing. Do not assume the iconic rounded pyramid can be summited.","source":"yucatantoday.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What is the Ruta Puuc, and are the Loltún caves worth it?","a":"The Ruta Puuc is the backroad ruin circuit south of Uxmal — Kabah (whose Codz Poop wears ~250 interlocking Chaac masks), Sayil''s three-story palace, the photogenic Arch of Labná, and quiet Xlapak. The Loltún caves cap it: a 700 m+ guided-only underground walk past cave paintings and \"musical\" ringing columns. A guided day neutralizes the heat, the remote road and the mandatory cave guide in one wrapper.","source":"yucatantoday.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is Uxmal safe right now?","a":"Yes — freely bookable. Uxmal is in Yucatán, one of only two Mexican states rated US State Dept Level 1 \"Exercise Normal Precautions,\" and the Puuc route itself is low-crime. Standard urban precautions apply in Mérida; the planning items on the route are heat and remoteness, not crime.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Uxmal and on the Puuc route?","a":"Heat and remoteness, not crime. Uxmal''s plazas are fully exposed limestone with almost no shade, and the Ruta Puuc runs long stretches with no fuel, water or medical services between sites. Time the visit for early morning or late afternoon, carry 1.5–2 L of water per person plus a hat and SPF, and leave Muna with a full tank; the nearest hospital is Mérida, ~1h15 north.","source":"yucatantoday.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"jsonld_type":"TouristAttraction","meta_title":"Uxmal & the Ruta Puuc: UNESCO Maya City Guide (2026) | TravelWell.World","search_language":"en","local_keywords":["Uxmal Ruta Puuc","Pirámide del Adivino","espectáculo de luz y sonido Uxmal","Grutas de Loltún visita guiada","haciendas Ruta Puuc","Kabah Codz Poop"],"long_tail_en":["Uxmal ruins guide 2026","Uxmal from Mérida day trip","Ruta Puuc Kabah Sayil Labná itinerary","Uxmal light and sound show tickets","Uxmal vs Chichén Itzá less crowded"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-06"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["culture_heritage","expedition","culinary"],"ultra":[{"name":"Chablé Yucatán","tier":"ultra","earning_path":"Virtuoso / Fora","note":"#13 World''s Best Hotels 2023; 3,400+ tequila bottles; ~30 min Mérida","source":"https://www.virtuoso.com/travel/luxury-hotels/15452675/chable-yucatan | Accessed 2026-07-06"},{"name":"Hacienda Temozón (Luxury Collection)","tier":"ultra","earning_path":"Virtuoso / Marriott STARS / Fora / MoR","note":"28 rooms; ~35 min Uxmal — natural Puuc base","source":"https://www.travelweekly.com/Hotels/Abala-Mexico/Hacienda-Temozon-Luxury-Collection-p51093491 | Accessed 2026-07-06"},{"name":"Hacienda Santa Rosa (Luxury Collection)","tier":"ultra","earning_path":"Virtuoso / Marriott STARS / MoR","note":"intimate 11 rooms","source":"https://www.letstraveltomexico.com/yucatan-haciendas/ | Accessed 2026-07-06"},{"name":"The Lodge at Uxmal","tier":"premier","earning_path":"Host FIT / MoR","note":"on-gate, walk to ruins"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Uxmal, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":20.3597,"lng":-89.7714}}'::jsonb, 116),
  ('valladolid-mexico', '10S', 'Valladolid', 'Mexico', 'Valladolid Yucatán', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Yucatán (Mérida & Chichén Itzá)', '{"expedition","culture","culinary"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["1543 colonial city + Pueblo Magico (2012), ~150 km from both Merida and Cancun; mid-peninsula base","Cenote Zaci in the heart of town (short staircase, park); swimmable, free w/ ~100 MXN restaurant","Cenote Suytun ~5 km E - iconic single light-beam on stone platform ~1-3 PM; ~250 MXN (230 online), 9 AM-5 PM","Cenote Oxman on a working hacienda - deep sinkhole + roots + rope swing + pool; 150 MXN (350 w/ lunch)","Ek Balam ~30 min N - CLIMBABLE 32 m acropolis (unlike Chichen), intricate stucco; ~170 MXN cash only"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"basic hospitals in town; nearest full trauma care Merida (~2 hr W, Star Medica/Clinica de Merida) or Cancun (~2 hr E, Hospiten/Amerimed) or air-evac","advisory_level":"L1","book_enabled":true,"air_access_verified":"yes - ~2 hr from MID Merida and ~2 hr from CUN Cancun (~150 km from each)","heat":"intense Yucatan sun - visit cenotes/Ek Balam at 9 AM opening; carry water + SPF; heat exhaustion risk at open ruins","cenote":"Zaci/Suytun/Oxman = swim/snorkel, NO lifeguard; life jackets (mandatory posture for non-swimmers/children); shower off sunscreen; slick platforms (Suytun) + rope swing (Oxman) - jump only where directed","dive_spine":"DISTINGUISH swim/snorkel (no cert) vs GUIDED cavern dive (certified cavern guide, light zone) vs CAVE dive (TECHNICAL - full cave cert, overhead, silt-out - FLAG HARD, never blur). Yucatan = world''s longest flooded caves (Ox-Bel-Ha ~269 km)","hyperbaric_no_fly":"nearest chambers on coast ~2+ hr (SSS/DAN Cancun, Playa, Cozumel; SSS Merida ~2 hr W); interior Yucatan has NO adjacent chamber - multi-hour evac for cave/cavern diving; DAN = nearest hospital first; observe no-fly 18-24 hr after multi-day/repetitive dives; carry DAN insurance","malaria":"effectively none in tourist zone","dengue":"active in Yucatan 2026; chikungunya/Zika circulate - use repellent","water":"bottled/purified only","hurricane":"Jun-Nov"},"timing":{"inflection_curve_start":"late September (winter/dry-season beds harden for Nov-Apr) / early February (Chichen spring-equinox halo)","peak":"dry season Nov-Apr; acute spikes = Chichen spring-equinox halo ~Mar 20-21 (closest boutique-bed base) + Dia de Muertos/Hanal Pixan late Oct-Nov 2","fire_date":"2026-09-14 (winter/dry-season campaign) and 2027-01-25 (spring-equinox halo push) - both curve-start minus 1-2 wks","shoulder":"May + Oct","green":"Jun-Sep (heat/humidity peak, hurricane-season afternoon rain) - cenotes at 9 AM opening","booking_lead":"boutique/casona beds weeks-to-months for Nov-Apr; equinox halo + Dia de Muertos = tight, book months ahead; cenote/Ek Balam/Cuzama tours on-site or a day out","off_season_specials":"green window: position as cool-off cenote base (Zaci/Suytun/Oxman + Cuzama/Homun) + slow-travel colonial alt to hot coast; bundle guided cavern-dive intro","event_peaks":"Dia de Muertos/Hanal Pixan (late Oct-Nov 2) = signature cultural peak; Chichen spring-equinox halo ~Mar 20-21; Semana Santa; Christmas-New Year","note":"sharpen on live tracking - confirm 2026 Hanal Pixan dates + 2027 equinox date; boutique inventory thin, sells out","sources":["https://www.lugaresturisticosenmexico.com/en/valladolid-yucatan-pueblo-magico/","https://thehaphazardtraveler.com/valladolid-yucatan-mexico/","https://www.dreambigtravelfarblog.com/blog/cenote-suytun"]},"jewels":[{"name":"Cenote Zací (in-town)","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"essential","bookable":"entry on site (free w/ ~100 MXN restaurant) + combo tour","commission_path":"DMC + Viator affiliate (entry non-commissionable)","source":"https://cenotesworld.com/en/cenotes-in-Valladolid-Pueblo-Magico-Yucatan/Cenote-Zaci/","timing":"dry season Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"a swimmable sinkhole a 2-min walk from the main square, in a public park; the only in-town cenote, gentlest first-swim","si":"expedition","blurb":"a swimmable sinkhole a 2-min walk from the main square, in a public park; the only in-town cenote, gentlest first-swim","when":"dry season Nov-Apr","commission":"DMC + Viator affiliate (entry non-commissionable)"},{"name":"Cenote Suytun (iconic light-beam)","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"essential","bookable":"entry ~250 MXN (230 online) + combo tour","commission_path":"DMC + Viator affiliate","source":"https://www.dreambigtravelfarblog.com/blog/cenote-suytun","timing":"dry season Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the region''s most photographed cenote — a single beam of light falls on a central stone platform","si":"expedition","blurb":"the region''s most photographed cenote — a single beam of light falls on a central stone platform","when":"dry season Nov-Apr","commission":"DMC + Viator affiliate"},{"name":"Cenote Oxman (hacienda sinkhole + rope swing)","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"essential","bookable":"150 MXN (350 w/ pool + lunch)","commission_path":"DMC + Viator affiliate","source":"https://cenotefinder.com/cenotes-in-mexico/valladolid-cenotes/","timing":"dry season Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"deep sinkhole draped in roots on a working hacienda, pool + restaurant, quieter","si":"expedition","blurb":"deep sinkhole draped in roots on a working hacienda, pool + restaurant, quieter","when":"dry season Nov-Apr","commission":"DMC + Viator affiliate"},{"name":"Cuzamá / Homún cenote country (horse-cart route)","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"essential","bookable":"on-site cart ~400 MXN (up to 4) + guided day tour; vet operator for animal welfare","commission_path":"DMC + Viator affiliate","source":"https://www.offpathtravels.com/cenotes-cuzama/","timing":"dry season Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"three-cenote railway horse-cart route through the meteor-crater Ring of Cenotes; Homún offers gentler truck/bike alternatives — vet operator for animal welfare","si":"expedition","blurb":"three-cenote railway horse-cart route through the meteor-crater Ring of Cenotes; Homún offers gentler truck/bike alternatives — vet operator for animal welfare","when":"dry season Nov-Apr","commission":"DMC + Viator affiliate"},{"name":"Guided cavern dive base","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"comfort","bookable":"professional cave/cavern dive operator (certified guide)","commission_path":"dive-operator commission on application + DAN insurance affiliate","source":"https://travelyucatan.com/cave-and-cenote-diving/","timing":"dry season Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Valladolid/Yucatán interior as a cavern-dive base with certified operators","si":"expedition","blurb":"Valladolid/Yucatán interior as a cavern-dive base with certified operators","when":"dry season Nov-Apr","commission":"dive-operator commission on application + DAN insurance affiliate"},{"name":"Ek Balam ruins (climbable acropolis) + Cenote X''Canche","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","tier":"essential","bookable":"~170 MXN cash + guided tour","commission_path":"DMC + Viator affiliate (entry non-commissionable, cash-only)","source":"https://thehaphazardtraveler.com/ek-balam/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"a Maya city 30 min N whose 32 m acropolis you can still climb, with rare intricate stucco façades; X''Canche swim 1.6 km away","si":"culture","blurb":"a Maya city 30 min N whose 32 m acropolis you can still climb, with rare intricate stucco façades; X''Canche swim 1.6 km away","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC + Viator affiliate (entry non-commissionable, cash-only)"},{"name":"Calzada de los Frailes + San Bernardino convent","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","tier":"essential","bookable":"free walk / guided colonial tour (convent evening sound-and-light)","commission_path":"walking-tour DMC + affiliate","source":"https://www.lugaresturisticosenmexico.com/en/valladolid-yucatan-pueblo-magico/","timing":"dry season Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the pastel colonial spine of the Pueblo Mágico — a photogenic street of restored façades leading to the 16th-c. convent","si":"culture","blurb":"the pastel colonial spine of the Pueblo Mágico — a photogenic street of restored façades leading to the 16th-c. convent","when":"dry season Nov-Apr","commission":"walking-tour DMC + affiliate"},{"name":"Casa de los Venados (folk-art house-museum)","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","tier":"essential","bookable":"donation-entry guided tour","commission_path":"cultural-tour affiliate (donation non-commissionable)","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/HotelsNear-g499453-d1863475-Casa_de_los_Venados-Valladolid_Yucatan_Peninsula.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"a private home + gallery holding 3,000+ pieces of Mexican folk & contemporary art — a singular cultural stop","si":"culture","blurb":"a private home + gallery holding 3,000+ pieces of Mexican folk & contemporary art — a singular cultural stop","when":"year-round","commission":"cultural-tour affiliate (donation non-commissionable)"},{"name":"Cochinita pibil in its heartland","si_tag":"Culinary","status":"future","tier":"comfort","bookable":"food-tour + boutique stay","commission_path":"food-tour affiliate + host boutique booking","source":"https://cenotefinder.com/cenotes-in-mexico/valladolid-cenotes/","timing":"dry season Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Valladolid is core Yucatecan-cuisine country — slow-roast cochinita pibil, longaniza, marquesitas; pair with a boutique-colonial stay","si":"culinary","blurb":"Valladolid is core Yucatecan-cuisine country — slow-roast cochinita pibil, longaniza, marquesitas; pair with a boutique-colonial stay","when":"dry season Nov-Apr","commission":"food-tour affiliate + host boutique booking"}],"faq":[{"q":"Which cenotes should I visit from Valladolid?","a":"Start with the three signatures. Zací is a swimmable sinkhole a 2-minute walk from the main square (free with a ~100 MXN restaurant meal) and the gentlest first swim; Suytun (~5 km east, ~250 MXN, open 9 AM–5 PM) delivers the iconic single light-beam onto its stone platform around 1–3 PM; and Oxman (150 MXN, or 350 with pool and lunch) is a deep, root-draped hacienda cenote with a rope swing. The Cuzamá/Homún horse-cart cenote country (~400 MXN/cart) adds a fourth day.","source":"dreambigtravelfarblog.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Can you climb the ruins at Ek Balam?","a":"Yes — its 32 m acropolis is climbable, which sets Ek Balam apart from Chichén Itzá, where El Castillo has been off-limits since 2008. The site (~30 min north) has rare, intricate stucco façades and a swimmable cenote, X''Canche, 1.6 km away; entry is ~170 MXN, cash only, with no ATM on site.","source":"thehaphazardtraveler.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is Valladolid a good base for the region?","a":"Yes — it is the mid-peninsula base the buses skip. Founded in 1543 and a Pueblo Mágico since 2012, it sits ~150 km from both Mérida and Cancún, ~40 min from Chichén Itzá, with a real layered bed market of boutique hotels, restored colonial casonas and haciendas — the slow-travel, colonial-romance alternative to the hot coast.","source":"thehaphazardtraveler.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What should I eat in Valladolid?","a":"This is core Yucatecan-cuisine country — slow-roast cochinita pibil, longaniza sausage and marquesita crêpes, amplified during the Hanal Pixán season. It pairs naturally with a boutique-colonial stay and an evening on the Calzada de los Frailes.","source":"cenotefinder.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"Is Valladolid safe right now?","a":"Yes — freely bookable. Valladolid is in Yucatán, one of only two Mexican states rated US State Dept Level 1 \"Exercise Normal Precautions.\" Take normal precautions; the town has only basic hospitals, so for serious care the nearest full trauma centers are Mérida or Cancún, each ~2 hr away — carry travel-medical insurance.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at the cenotes?","a":"Heat and unguarded water. The cenotes and Ek Balam are best at the 9 AM opening before the heat builds; the cenotes are swim/snorkel with no lifeguards, so use provided life jackets (mandatory posture for non-swimmers and children), shower off sunscreen first, and mind slick stone platforms and rope swings. Drink bottled water only.","source":"dreambigtravelfarblog.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is cenote diving safe here?","a":"Yes when the three tiers are never blurred. Swimming and snorkeling need no certification; a guided cavern dive stays in the daylight zone with a certified cave-guide leading; true cave diving is a technical, Full-Cave-only discipline in some of the world''s longest flooded caves (Ox-Bel-Ha ~269 km) and is never sold to an uncertified diver. Carry DAN insurance, observe no-fly for 18–24 h, and know the nearest chamber is ~2+ hr away on the coast.","source":"travelyucatan.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Valladolid Mexico 2026: Cenotes Suytun, Zací, Oxman & Ek Balam","meta_description":"Valladolid is a Yucatán Pueblo Mágico + cenote base — swim Zací, Suytun (light beam) and Oxman, climb Ek Balam, walk Calzada de los Frailes. Boutique stays, fees, cenote-dive safety.","slug":"valladolid-mexico","primary_keyword":"Valladolid Yucatán","long_tail":["cenotes Valladolid Suytun Zací Oxman","Cenote Suytun light beam best time","Ek Balam ruins from Valladolid","Valladolid Pueblo Mágico things to do","Cuzamá Homún horse cart cenotes","Valladolid boutique hotels"],"search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["cenotes Valladolid","Cenote Suytun rayo de luz","Cenote Zací Valladolid","Cenote Oxman hacienda","ruinas Ek Balam Valladolid","Valladolid Pueblo Mágico qué hacer","cenotes Cuzamá Homún","Calzada de los Frailes","cochinita pibil Valladolid","hoteles boutique Valladolid"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-06"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"culture","status":"future"},{"si":"culinary","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Coqui Coqui Valladolid (Meson de Malleville)","tier":"premier-luxury BOUTIQUE (straight - design/intimacy/place, not 5-star resort)","why":"wellness/perfumery boutique brand in a colonial property; sell on soul not square footage","earning":"FIT/consortia (Fora/Virtuoso where property participates), commission on application","mor":"host MoR on stay + private tour; cenote/site fees non-commissionable","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/HotelsList-Valladolid-Boutique-Hotels-zfp12515607.html"},{"name":"Le Muuch Hotel Boutique","tier":"premier-luxury boutique (21 rooms, boho-chic design)","why":"intimate design boutique in the colonial core","earning":"FIT/consortia, commission on application","mor":"host MoR on stay","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/HotelsList-Valladolid-Boutique-Hotels-zfp12515607.html"},{"name":"Chable Yucatan (Merida circuit, ~2 hr W) - nearest TRUE ultra","tier":"ultra-luxury (Leading Hotels of the World)","why":"200-yr San Antonio hacienda, 750 acres, spa beside a sacred cenote, ~30 min from MID; base for private-guided Valladolid/cenote/Ek Balam/Chichen ultra day excursions","earning":"FIT/consortia (Virtuoso/Fora), commission on application","mor":"host MoR on stay + private tour","source":"https://www.lhw.com/hotel/Chable-Yucatan-Chochola-Merida-Mexico"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Valladolid, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":20.6896,"lng":-88.2011}}'::jsonb, 117),
  ('valle-de-guadalupe-mexico', '10S', 'Valle de Guadalupe, Mexico', 'Mexico', '*If it''s a Grenache poured at the vine that', 'live', 'verified', 'restaurant', 'Baja California (Valle de Guadalupe & Ensenada)', '{"culinary"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Mexico''s premier wine country — 100+ wineries along the Ruta del Vino, producing >90% of Mexican wine.","Baja Med farm-to-table anchors: Deckman''s en el Mogor (Michelin), Fauna, Corazón de Tierra, Finca Altozano.","Fiestas de la Vendimia (August) is the peak: 80+ wineries, 160+ labels, paella competition, pairing dinners.","Design wine-lodges: Banyan Tree Veya (30 villas, on-site Grenache winery), Encuentro/Endémico, Bruma.","Inside the Ensenada carve-out — Baja California is US L3 but the advisory names Ensenada NO-restriction."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","book_enabled":true,"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","consent_flow":{"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","disclosure_required":true,"renders":"full verbatim live US State Dept advisory for Mexico (Baja California section + named carve-outs + ''If you decide to travel''), pulled live, plus traveler acknowledgment","wording_status":"hook set only — final consent language PENDING compliance-attorney sign-off"},"state_dept_carveout":"Ensenada/Tijuana/Rosarito no-restriction","trauma":"Ensenada/Tijuana → San Diego US cross-border evacuation (US-standard trauma care) — a structural cross-border advantage","drink_driving":"always a designated driver / guided wine tour — never self-drive the tasting circuit","rural_road":"Hwy 3 + winery access roads are rural, partly unlit; daylight transfers only, no rural night driving","water":"bottled/filtered","air_access_verified":"Tijuana International (TIJ) via Cross Border Xpress (CBX) pedestrian bridge from San Diego (Otay Mesa), then ~1–1.5 hr drive on Hwy 3; or San Ysidro/Otay Mesa land crossing; Ensenada as coastal gateway. San Diego → Valle ~1h52m + border.","source":"https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/traveladvisories/traveladvisories/mexico-travel-advisory.html","accessed":"2026-07-07"},"timing":{"peak":"Fiestas de la Vendimia harvest festival — early-to-late August 2026 (Aug 5–23 window), within a warm/dry Jul–Sep harvest season","curve_start":"early-to-mid July (Vendimia programming + ticketing go live, harvest window opens)","inflection":"early-to-mid July","fire_date":"2026-06-20 to 2026-06-30 (curve-start − 1–2 weeks; fire before disclosure + scarce Vendimia lodging/tickets lock)","shoulder":"spring Apr–Jun (bud-break to pre-harvest) and fall late-Sep–Oct (post-harvest, quieter cellars)","low_season":"winter Dec–Feb (quiet trough; design/romance demand persists; Viñadas shoulder programming expanding fill)"},"jewels":[{"name":"Monte Xanic","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"guided-wine-tour rung (DMC)","source":"https://bajasocietytours.com/blog/monte-xanic-valle-de-guadalupe/","timing":"Fiestas de la Vendimia harvest festival — early-to-late August 2026 , within a warm/dry Jul–Sep harvest season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the disciplined benchmark red producer, ~60,000 cases across four labels; guided tasting is a must-book","si":"culinary","blurb":"the disciplined benchmark red producer, ~60,000 cases across four labels; guided tasting is a must-book","when":"Fiestas de la Vendimia harvest festival — early-to-late August 2026 , within a warm/dry Jul–Sep harvest season","commission":"guided-wine-tour rung (DMC)"},{"name":"Adobe Guadalupe (winery + B&B + Azteca horses)","si_tag":"Culinary/GEA","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"boutique lodging + guided-tour + activity","source":"https://explorenowornever.com/valle-de-guadalupe-wineries/","timing":"Fiestas de la Vendimia harvest festival — early-to-late August 2026 , within a warm/dry Jul–Sep harvest season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"colon